From: theodotdot <59372255+theodotdot@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: ddic-ch13726a: restore LPM mode when a brightness write fails

The brightness path clears MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM before the DCS write and restores it
only on success, so a failed write leaves the link in HS mode for every later
write. This panel answers EINVAL while still applying the value, so one failure is
enough to change how the following writes are transmitted.

Restore the flag on the error path as well. Source: ours, sent to ROCKNIX, whose
copy of this driver carries the bug.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ddic-ch13726a.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ddic-ch13726a.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ddic-ch13726a.c
@@ -269,8 +269,11 @@
 	dsi->mode_flags &= ~MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM;
 
 	ret = mipi_dsi_dcs_set_display_brightness(dsi, brightness);
-	if (ret < 0)
+	if (ret < 0) {
+		/* Leave the flag as it was: the next write must not inherit HS mode */
+		dsi->mode_flags |= MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM;
 		return ret;
+	}
 
 	dsi->mode_flags |= MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM;
 
